<title>BELGIUM: FRENCH PIXTECH SAYS TO LEAD EU CONTRACT.</title>
<headline>FRENCH PIXTECH SAYS TO LEAD EU CONTRACT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>French firm PixTech said on Friday it would lead a $3.0 million contract granted by the European Union to develop the company's flat-screen technology.</p>
<p>Under the contract PixTech would lead a consortium of European companies. Revenues would amount to $3.0 million over an 18-month period, of which PixTech's share would be $900,000.</p>
<p>&quot;This...contract will allow us to develop the successful R&amp;D (research and development) partnerships established with SAES Getters and Rhone Poulenc within the framework of our previous European Union contract,&quot; PixTech's executive vice-president Francis Courreges said in a statement.</p>
<p>PixTech was launched on the Brussels-based pan-European growth stocks market Easdaq in February. It is also quoted on the Nasdaq excahnge in New York.</p>
<p>SAES Getters is an Italian electronic components maker and Rhone Poulenc SA a French chemical company.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
